{"toolCallId":"call_3c739cd946f94f60b86f8c4883c8412b","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/recommend-level-quiet`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: P0/P1/P2] |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The recommend-level script prints a 17-line report, so a caller that needs only the level cannot parse the answer. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\n\n### Purpose\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: One-sentence outcome statement. What does success look like?]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. GOOD: Add a `--quiet` flag that prints only the recommended-level line. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 1]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 2]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Deliverable 3]\n\n### Out of Scope\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 1] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Excluded item 2] - [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: why]\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: path/to/file.js] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Modify/Create/Delete] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With `--quiet`, stdout holds exactly one line that starts with `Recommended Level:`. WEAK: The flag should work well. -->\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-002 | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Requirement description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: How to verify it's done] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: `recommend-level.sh --quiet --loc 500 --files 15` prints one line and exits 0. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n\n- **SC-001**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Primary measurable outcome]\n- **SC-002**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Secondary measurable outcome]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Name one dependency and one risk. Give each a concrete mitigation. GOOD: A caller parses the level line and breaks when the label changes. Mitigation: keep the label stable and test it. WEAK: There may be some risk. -->\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: System/API] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: What if blocked] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Fallback plan] |\n| Risk | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Risk description] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: High/Med/Low] | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Mitigation strategy] |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n<!-- FILL: Write each open question as one line. Write `None` when nothing blocks. GOOD: Does `--quiet` also suppress warnings on stderr? Decision: no, stderr is unchanged. WEAK: Edge cases are unclear. -->\n\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 1 requiring clarification]\n- [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Question 2 requiring clarification]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports an Overall Completion percentage but ends with an unconditional exit 0, so a CI step that wants to fail a thin packet has to parse the report text. A --min-percent option moves that decision into the exit status.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P2 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `HEAD (detached; no branch created)` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints `Overall Completion: N%` in text mode and `\"overall_completion\": N` in JSON mode, then ends with an unconditional `exit 0`. A CI step or wrapper that wants to fail a packet below a threshold has to capture the report, find the percentage line and parse the number out of it, and every caller writes that parsing again.\n\n### Purpose\nA caller passes `--min-percent <N>` and reads the answer from the exit status, while the report text stays byte-for-byte identical to what it prints today.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Parse `--min-percent <N>` in the section 8 option loop, next to the existing `--file` arm.\n- Reject a value that is not an integer from 0 to 100 with the script's existing `ERROR:`-on-stderr and exit 1 form.\n- Exit 3 after the report when the reported completion is below N, and exit 0 otherwise.\n- List the option in `show_help`, in the file's usage header and in the exit-code footer.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- The percentage arithmetic and the report layout - the flag reads the value the report already prints, so neither changes.\n- A short alias or an environment variable - the request names one long option, and callers already pass flags.\n- The other scripts in `runtime/cli/spec/` - `validate.sh` and its siblings are untouched.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Add the option, its validation, the help text and the threshold exit |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | `--min-percent <N>` is accepted and the report is unchanged | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 50 <folder>` and `calculate-completeness.sh <folder>` print identical stdout and stderr; only the exit status may differ |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N | A folder whose report prints `Overall Completion: 20%` run with `--min-percent 50` exits 3 |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported completion is at or above N, including exactly N | The same folder with `--min-percent 20` exits 0, and a run without the flag exits 0 as it does today |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-004 | A value that is not an integer from 0 to 100 exits 1 with an `ERROR:` line on stderr and no report | `--min-percent abc`, `--min-percent -1`, `--min-percent 101` and a bare `--min-percent` each exit 1 and print no results block |\n| REQ-005 | The help text and the exit-code footer document the option and code 3 | `--help` output contains the `--min-percent <N>` line, and the footer lists `3` with its meaning |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: On a fixture folder that prints below the threshold, `--min-percent 50` exits 3 while the plain run exits 0, and both write the same bytes to stdout.\n- **SC-002**: On the same folder, `--min-percent` set to the printed percentage exits 0 and one point above it exits 3.\n- **SC-003**: `validate.sh --strict` on this packet prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, which the script already requires | Low - the flag adds no new dependency and the existing check exits 1 without it | Leave the `command -v bc` guard where it is, ahead of the calculation |\n| Risk | A caller reads exit 3 as a crash and aborts its run | Medium | Document 3 in `--help` and the footer, and keep 1 for real errors so the two stay distinguishable |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns an unvalidated comparison into a silent exit before the report | Medium | Validate N before the calculation, and write the final branch as an `if` that always ends in an explicit `exit 0` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does the flag gate `--file` mode, where the report prints `Completion:` instead of `Overall Completion:`? Decision: it compares the percentage the report presents for the requested scope - the single file's `Completion` in `--file` mode, `Overall Completion` otherwise - so the flag and the status line never disagree.\n- Does `--json` change? Decision: no. The JSON body stays as it is and callers read the exit status.\n- What does a non-integer N do? Decision: exit 1 with an `ERROR:` line, matching the script's other argument errors, so 3 means only \"below the threshold\".\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":27,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":28}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
