Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the section 8 option loop, the two output functions and the trailing `exit 0` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`). Verify: `rg -n 'exit 0|--file\\|-f'` prints the `--file` arm and the final exit\n- [ ] T002 Build a throwaway fixture packet with `mktemp -d` and enough placeholder lines in `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` to land the report well below the threshold. Verify: the plain run prints `Overall Completion: <N>%` and exits 0\n- [ ] T003 [P] Confirm `bc` is installed, since the script exits 1 without it. Verify: `command -v bc` exits 0\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` to the section 3 globals and a `--min-percent) MIN_PERCENT=\"$2\"; shift 2 ;;` arm to the section 8 option loop (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent'` prints the case arm\n- [ ] T005 Validate the parsed value after the loop: an integer from 0 to 100, or `ERROR: --min-percent requires an integer from 0 to 100` on stderr with exit 1, before the `bc` check and the calculation (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`). Verify: `--min-percent abc`, `-1`, `101` and a bare `--min-percent` each exit 1 and print no results block\n- [ ] T006 Add the exit gate after the output call: exit 3 when the presented percentage is below `MIN_PERCENT`, else exit 0, written as an `if` that always ends in an explicit `exit 0` (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`). Verify: `--min-percent 100` on the fixture exits 3\n- [ ] T007 Document the option in `show_help`, the file's usage header and the exit-code footer (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`). Verify: `--help` prints the `--min-percent <N>` line and the footer lists exit 3\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Capture stdout from the plain run and from `--min-percent 50` on the same fixture, then diff them. Verify: `diff` prints nothing and the two exit statuses are 0 and 3\n- [ ] T009 Run the boundary pair: N at the printed percentage and N one point above it. Verify: the first exits 0 and the second exits 3\n- [ ] T010 Repeat with `--file` and `--json`. Verify: `--file` with a threshold above the file's `Completion` exits 3, and the `--json` body is byte-identical to the unflagged run\n- [ ] T011 Run `validate.sh --strict` on this packet. Verify: it prints `RESULT: PASSED`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":11,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":19}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_bcd3f51a69ca488b97806ab992aa5bb8","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one output branch. Prove it with a line count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `rg -n 'quiet' recommend-level.sh` prints the new branch before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `recommend-level.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup reads the current output. Implementation adds the branch. Verification counts lines. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `--quiet` prints 1 line. The default prints 17. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\nN/A — record any testing beyond the verification tasks in `tasks.md` here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\nN/A — record dependencies beyond the components named in the architecture here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: the default output changes. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\nN/A — record rollback steps beyond reverting the scoped change here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one option arm, one validation guard and one exit-status branch to calculate-completeness.sh, then prove the report bytes and the 0/1/3 exit codes on a throwaway fixture packet.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.3 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None |\n| **Storage** | None; the script writes per-file stats to a temp directory it removes on exit |\n| **Testing** | Direct invocations against a `mktemp -d` fixture folder, plus `validate.sh --strict` |\n\n### Overview\nThe change is confined to `calculate-completeness.sh`. The section 8 option loop gains a `--min-percent <N>` arm that sets a new global, a guard rejects a value outside 0-100 before any counting starts, and a branch after the output call exits 3 when the percentage the report presented is below N. Proof compares stdout byte for byte across the plain and flagged runs, then reads the exit status at the threshold, one point above it and for each invalid input.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] Tests passing (if applicable)\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nOther: a single script with one option gate at its exit.\n\n### Key Components\n- **`calculate-completeness.sh` section 8 option loop**: the `case` that already reads `--file`, `--verbose`, `--json` and `--quality`; it gains the `--min-percent` arm and the guard that follows the loop.\n- **`show_help` and the file header**: the usage block and the exit-code footer, which become the discoverable contract for the flag.\n- **The final exit branch**: the one place exit 3 is raised, after the report has already been written.\n\n### Data Flow\n`argv` enters the option loop, which sets `MIN_PERCENT` and leaves `SPEC_FOLDER` and `SINGLE_FILE` as they are. The guard rejects a bad value before the `bc` check and the calculation, so no report is printed on that path. The calculation fills `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` for a folder, or the single-file stats file for `--file`. The output function prints the report unchanged. The gate then compares that same presented percentage to `MIN_PERCENT` and exits 3 or 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nCreate a fixture packet under `mktemp -d` holding a `spec.md`, `plan.md` and `tasks.md` with enough placeholder lines to land the reported percentage well below the threshold, and delete it when the runs finish. Record the plain run's stdout and exit 0 as the baseline. Then run the flagged form against the same folder, diff the two stdout captures, and read the exit statuses: 3 below the threshold, 0 at exactly the printed percentage, 3 one point above it, and 1 for `abc`, `-1`, `101` and a bare `--min-percent`. Repeat once with `--file` and once with `--json` to confirm the gate follows the presented percentage and the JSON body is unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n`bash` and `bc`. The script already checks for `bc` and exits 1 without it, and the flag introduces no new package or tool.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: the run without the flag changes its output or its exit status. Revert the single commit that touches the script. The option is additive, so nothing else depends on it yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":17,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":24}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
